<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roberto Durán</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1951">1951</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roberto Durán is a Panamanian boxer, nicknamed Manos de Piedra (Hands of Stone), widely regarded as one of the greatest lightweights of all time. He won world titles in four weight divisions between 1972 and 1989, and his victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">Sugar</a> Ray Leonard in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a> in 1980 made him a national hero, although he lost the rematch later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roberto-duran.jpg" alt="Roberto Durán" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jim Accordino · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roberto-Duran-1994_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
